.TH SLIDES 1 "July 2026" "c-slides v@VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
slides \- markdown-to-slides presentation tool
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B slides
[\fIoptions\fR] \fIpresentation.md\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B slides
renders a Markdown file as a slideshow presentation with live preview,
animated transitions, and export to PDF, PNG, SVG, GIF, and JPG formats.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-palette " \fIname\fR"
Choose a color palette. Supported values: dark, rose, monokai, nord, light,
blue, ambercat, dracula, gruvbox, catppuccin, tokyo-night.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-font-family " \fIstr\fR"
Set the font family (e.g. 'Arial', 'JetBrains Mono').
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-font-scale " \fInum\fR"
Scale the font size (e.g. 1.2).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-export " \fItype\fR"
Export slides to the specified format. Supported types:
.RS
pdf  \- Portable Document Format
png  \- Portable Network Graphics (one file per slide)
svg  \- Scalable Vector Graphics (one file per slide)
gif  \- Animated GIF (all slides in one file)
jpg  \- JPEG image (one file per slide)
.RE
.TP
.BR \-er ", " \-\-export-res " \fIWxH\fR"
Set the export resolution (e.g. 1920x1080). Default: 1080x1080.
.TP
.BR \-sl ", " \-\-slide " \fInum\fR"
Select a specific slide to export (0-indexed). Only valid for png, svg,
and jpg export.
.TP
.BR \-\-bg " \fIhex\fR"
Override the background color (e.g. '#0f0f23').
.TP
.BR \-\-title " \fIhex\fR"
Override the title color (e.g. '#ff6b6b').
.TP
.BR \-\-text " \fIhex\fR"
Override the body text color (e.g. '#c0caf5').
.TP
.BR \-\-accent " \fIhex\fR"
Override the accent color (e.g. '#7aa2f7').
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a brief usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display the version number and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Present a slideshow:
.RS
slides presentation.md
.RE
.TP
Export to PDF:
.RS
slides \-e pdf presentation.md
.RE
.TP
Export to PNG at 1920x1080:
.RS
slides \-e png \-\-export-res 1920x1080 presentation.md
.RE
.TP
Export slide 2 as JPEG:
.RS
slides \-e jpg \-\-slide 1 presentation.md
.RE
.TP
Export animated GIF:
.RS
slides \-e gif presentation.md
.RE
.SH MARKDOWN SYNTAX
Slides are separated by a horizontal rule
(\fB---\fR or \fB***\fR) on its own line.
.SS Text formatting
.TP
.B *italic* or _italic_
italic
.TP
.B **bold** or __bold__
bold
.TP
.B ~~strikethrough~~
strikethrough
.TP
.B `code`
inline code
.SS Code blocks
Fenced code blocks with language identifier (e.g. ```c) are syntax-highlighted.
.SS Images
.RS
![alt text](image.png)
.RE
Local and remote images are supported. Animated GIF images play during
presentations and are rendered as static frames in exports.
.SS Lists
Unordered lists use \-, \*, or \+. Ordered lists use numbers followed by a dot.
.SS Tables
Standard Markdown tables with pipes and dashes are supported.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I presentation.md
Input Markdown file.
.TP
.I slide_N.pdf\|png\|svg\|jpg
Output files created by export commands (one per slide).
.TP
.I presentation.pdf\|gif
Output files created by PDF or GIF export (single file).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PKG_CONFIG_PATH
May need to be set on Windows to point to the MSYS2 pkg-config directory
(e.g. C:/msys64/mingw64/lib/pkgconfig).
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at https://github.com/xeland314/slides.c/issues.
.SH AUTHOR
Written by xeland314.
